<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Entitlements for DISTRIBUTION signing — Developer ID Application cert + hardened runtime +
    notarization (see eng/ci/sign-macos-app.sh, driven by .github/workflows/release.yml).

    Sibling file macos-resign.entitlements is the LOCAL ad-hoc variant; keep the two in sync.

    Why each key is needed:
      allow-jit / allow-unsigned-executable-memory
          The .NET runtime JITs. Hardened runtime blocks W+X memory without these.
      disable-library-validation
          MonoBundle's dylibs are signed as individual Mach-O files rather than sealed into a
          framework, and the WKWebView content process loads them; library validation would
          reject them as "not from the same team".

    Deliberately NOT set:
      com.apple.security.app-sandbox
          The app keeps its SQLite document store under ~/Library/Application Support and reads
          user-chosen files via NSOpenPanel; sandboxing would need a full entitlement audit and
          is only required for Mac App Store distribution, not for Developer ID + notarization.
      com.apple.security.get-task-allow
          Debug-only. Notarization REJECTS any binary carrying it.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-jit</key><true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.allow-unsigned-executable-memory</key><true/>
    <key>com.apple.security.cs.disable-library-validation</key><true/>
</dict>
</plist>
